# Every unwritten command exits NON-ZERO.
#
# A stub that returns 0 with a friendly "coming soon" is the worst of the
# options: a script driving it appears to succeed, and in this tool "appeared
# to succeed" can mean a provider was never installed, or a credential never
# stored, while the caller moves on.
#
# When one of these lines starts failing, it is because the command was
# implemented. That is the intended alarm — delete the line and write a real
# script for it.

! exec sal open
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal drift
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal providers create acme
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal providers remove acme
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal secrets set acme
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal secrets list
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal features list
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal features enable observer
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal features disable observer
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal observer open
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal observer tail
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal labs list
stderr 'not implemented yet'

! exec sal labs down
stderr 'not implemented yet'

# The error names the full command path, so a failure in a script says which
# invocation it came from.
! exec sal providers create acme
stderr 'sal providers create'
